# Bilingual UX/UI — ENG + VIE

Locales: **`en`** (ENG) and **`vi`** (VIE). Any UX/UI edit must update **both** in the same change.

## When this applies

- New or changed visible copy (labels, CTAs, nav, empty states, errors, captions)
- New UI surfaces, layout chrome, toggles, forms, calculators, guides
- Chapter overlays / localized content fields users can read

## Do

- Edit `src/i18n/ui.ts` for **both** `en` and `vi` keys together
- Keep `UiDict` keys in sync — no key present in only one locale
- For chapter text overlays, update ENG source + VIE overlay (`src/i18n/` + chapter locale data)
- QA both locales via `LocaleToggle` before considering the change done

## Don't

- Ship ENG-only or VIE-only strings
- Hardcode user-facing English (or Vietnamese) in components — use `t` / `useT` / `useLocale`
- Leave placeholder/`TODO` VIE while ENG is polished

## Checklist (before finish)

- [ ] Same keys in `ui.en` and `ui.vi`
- [ ] No hardcoded user-facing strings in JSX
- [ ] Spot-check ENG + VIE on the touched surface
